{{INSTANCE_INPUT}}

You can think of the final answer as a little form in JSON — nice and tidy so a script (or a human) can read it easily. Here's the shape to follow:

{
  "solution": [
    {
      "job": <loaf_id>,
      "machine": <oven_id>,
      "start": <start_time>,
      "end": <end_time>
    }
  ]
}

This sketch means: each object in the solution array is one loaf assigned to one oven, with a start time and an end time. Keep it casual: "job" is the loaf identifier, "machine" is the oven identifier, "start" is when that loaf goes into the oven, and "end" is when it comes out. Times are the scheduling times (same units as the instance).

This JSON block is just the expected shape — not the actual scheduled times. Also, please use the exact job and machine identifiers from the instance input; do not rename them or invent new labels. Valid identifiers look like plain numbers such as “1” or “23”, single capital letters like “A” or “B”, or a capital letter followed by digits like “A1” or “X7”.

